Primorskij Kraj).","","text","",""]]},"VCJSD":{"d":[["Distribution (Map 1). The nominotypical subspecies of A. squalida is one of the most widespread Afroracotis taxa. It was described from Nigeria and had earlier been recorded from Bioko, Cameroon, Central African Republic, DRC, Ghana, Ivory Coast, Kenya, Malawi, Mozambique, Republic of the Congo, RSA, Sierra Leone, Tanzania, Uganda and Zimbabwe. The specimens examined in this study from Burkina Faso, Burundi, Guinea, Liberia, Togo, Gabon, Zambia and Ethiopia represent new country records. It is worth noting that a single male specimen examined from southern Ethiopia displayed somewhat diverging morphology in the male genitalia expressed by the considerably longer diverticula of the vesica, especially the distal one which is ca. twice as long as in typical A. squalida specimens (Fig. 215). As the female individuals from Ethiopia do not show any morphological differences to other populations, and the DNA barcodes do not suggest the presence of genetically diverging populations throughout the entire range of the species, the single dissected Ethiopian male is treated here as A. squalida. Nevertheless, examination of further specimens from Ethiopia may prove the presence of a distinct taxon if constant differences in the genital morphology are confirmed.","","text","",""]]},"X9V3":{"d":[["China","","text","native",""]]},"XWY2":{"d":[["Tuamotus","21943","mrgid","",""]]},"Y77S":{"d":[["Afrotropical(Republic South Africa:Cape)","","text","",""]]},"YF9B":{"d":[["Angola","47955","mrgid","",""]]},"YXSV":{"d":[["Brazil","","text","",""]]},"YXT5":{"d":[["Venezuela, Brazil","","text","",""]]},"ZV64":{"d":[["Neotropical(Mexico:Chiapas)","","text","",""]]}}